{"skill":{"slug":"news-aggregator-skill","displayName":"News Aggregator Skill"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769420683107,"changelog":"Initial release of news-aggregator-skill:\n- Aggregates, filters, and deeply analyzes real-time news from 8 major sources including Hacker News, GitHub Trending, Product Hunt, and more.\n- Supports broad \"global scan\" and smart keyword expansion for user queries.\n- Adds deep fetching mode to extract article text (`--deep` flag).\n- Interactive menu system for user guidance via templates.\n- Smart time filtering and \"smart fill\" to ensure meaningful reports.\n- Responses formatted in Magazine/Newsletter style with deep interpretations (in Simplified Chinese).\n- Full reports automatically saved to `reports/` directory and presented to the user.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3503,"sha256":"81b8402bfa11711fb79eb774769a27c936ba619aa89b4f21c498c77e948eb9a3","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":5072,"sha256":"ac23cf08f189f8a588aebbfb0e90b356cfb087274e5aa545212255ac7513860d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":24,"sha256":"2c081c1999175987aca18adf80b955273f88cc96b4b188ace8b1991aaa971ca7","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/fetch_news.py","size":12403,"sha256":"1f6fc72ead386c4a8e9261e2d64fe643fa475cb1ceecbf58aecdb3aa2029d1dd","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"templates.md","size":2010,"sha256":"13b9954bef8ef9381fc4f69c32aca59c37ca2bc36d44d34d387662eaa0ee533d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2496,"sha256":"34b46719c336f1114d7201c148a20063936407dcee1491b43842544b8041341f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789019290978,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"ebdc1694c7725afece0de1e49b0f3ff470e4c034c228f6bcc756eb1de54c36ba","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/ebdc1694c7725afece0de1e49b0f3ff470e4c034c228f6bcc756eb1de54c36ba","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: news-aggregator-skill\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is classified as suspicious primarily due to prompt injection instructions found in `SKILL.md`. Specifically, the 'Smart Keyword Expansion' section explicitly instructs the AI agent to automatically expand and modify the user's input keywords (e.g., 'AI' -> 'AI,LLM,GPT,...') before executing the `fetch_news.py` script. While the stated intent is to broaden search results, this constitutes an instruction for the agent to override or augment user input, which is a form of prompt manipulation. Additionally, the `scripts/fetch_news.py` performs extensive web scraping, including fetching content from arbitrary article URLs if the `--deep` flag is used, which is a high-risk capability, though it appears to be aligned with the skill's stated purpose and lacks direct malicious indicators like exfiltration or arbitrary code execution.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160016044},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":95,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":18,"checkedAt":1789019290978},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a legitimate news aggregation skill, but its deep-fetch mode can retrieve arbitrary article URLs from untrusted feeds and save reports without enough containment or user control.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access is central to the skill, but unrestricted deep article fetching lacks an allowlist, private-address filtering, redirect controls, or explicit containment guidance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation instructions use a floating GitHub/NPX source and unpinned Python dependencies; this is a supply-chain reproducibility issue, but not evidence of malicious code in the artifact.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill uses broad natural-language triggers, asks the agent to expand keywords automatically, and requires full reports to be saved, which makes activation and side effects broader than a narrowly scoped news lookup.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill tells the agent to always write timestamped reports under reports/, which is disclosed but lacks opt-in, retention guidance, or a no-save mode; no cron, startup hook, memory poisoning, or backdoor persistence was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Fetching and summarizing news is coherent with the stated purpose, but deep mode follows externally supplied article URLs and passes extracted page text into agent analysis without a trust-boundary warning.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing if your agent runs inside a private network or has access to sensitive files, credentials, or internal services. Use it only in a constrained environment, avoid deep-fetch mode for untrusted sources, pin dependencies, and treat fetched article text and generated reports as untrusted content.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: The artifact supports the concern: fetch_url_content only checks that URLs start with http and requests follows redirects by default, so deep mode can request attacker-influenced destinations beyond the intended news sources.\n[T01] unexpected: The artifact supports the concern: deep mode extracts arbitrary article text and SKILL.md instructs the agent to use it for analysis, but does not say retrieved content is untrusted data whose instructions must be ignored.\n[T08] expected: The unpinned requests and beautifulsoup4 dependencies and floating NPX install are real reproducibility risks, but the package names and install pattern are not themselves malicious.\n[LP3] unexpected: The network-capable script is purpose-aligned, but the artifact does not define domain or permission boundaries for broad source fetching and deep article retrieval.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact requires every full report to be saved to reports/ with a timestamped filename, without an opt-in or no-save path.\n[RP1] expected: The README does document floating remote installation; this is a supply-chain caution rather than evidence that the reviewed artifact changes itself after installation.\n[AS3] expected: The cited README commands create and verify the skill installation path, not enumerate or read unrelated installed skills; this finding is downgraded.\n[RA2] expected: Copying the skill into a skills directory is normal installation persistence, and I found no cron job, startup script, service, or hidden cross-session execution.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-language output and China-focused sources are clearly visible in the README, SKILL.md, and templates; this is a user-preference limitation, not a security concern by itself.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad description and 'or similar' menu/help triggers could activate the skill on ordinary news requests, which matters because activation may cause network fetches and report writing.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789019290978}}}}}